{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "10418",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10418",
  "key": "AIN-95",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Persona] Review material changes and preserve corrections when forms regenerate",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User story"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "As a submission reviewer, I want to compare and activate regenerated forms so that document updates do not silently erase corrections or preserve stale approvals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Feedback coverage"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Original feedback: I6, B2, R4. I = insurer; B = broker; R = reinsurer; numbering follows the 20 points per persona in the user conversation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scope and existing implementation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Extend current services, generated-form workbench, commercial records and tests. These are outcome/verification gaps, not an assertion that every underlying capability is absent. Preserve existing working functionality and all broader parent obligations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing implementation owners: AIN-18, AIN-50, AIN-51. Existing tasks retain their original scope and hierarchy. Completed tasks are reuse evidence, not proof that this broader story is Done."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance criteria"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1. Pin source, prompt/generator/model, catalog, schema and semantic-binding versions; retain separate structural and data hashes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "2. Match fields and repeated records by stable semantic/entity IDs rather than labels or row positions; carry forward only compatible reviewed corrections."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "3. Present added, removed, conflicting, unit/cardinality and entity split/merge changes for resolution before activation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "4. Activation atomically selects the effective revision and marks affected quotes, pricing, capacity and approvals stale; historical replay never calls the LLM or overwrites prior artifacts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Required dependencies"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Required predecessor outcomes: AIN-87; final Jira key mapping follows below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Story-specific verification"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reorder two locations, change currency, remove a corrected field and retry activation concurrently; verify correct correction ownership, one effective revision and stale dependent approvals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Definition of Done"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1. All acceptance criteria and the story-specific verification scenario pass; link implementation tasks/PRs and record the reviewed source/package versions. A partial component or newly created ticket does not satisfy this story."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "2. Every changed UI workflow has executable Storybook play functions asserting user actions, observable results and exact submitted payloads, including success, validation, failure/retry, empty/loading, pagination and permission/revocation states where applicable. Document a reason for any nonapplicable state. Include keyboard and narrow-screen checks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "3. Fixture stories use isolated synthetic transports with accidental application writes blocked. Also run authenticated real-service journeys against isolated Docker databases/services for authorization, durable state, concurrency, idempotency and relevant money invariants. Backend-only work uses integration evidence linked to this story, not artificial UI."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "4. Attach ticket \u2192 component \u2192 Storybook story IDs \u2192 command/results mapping, regression evidence, API/database checks and known coverage gaps to Jira and TASK_HANDOFF.md. New failures have linked bug tickets and regressions; no unresolved failure of an acceptance criterion permits Done."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "5. Reconcile all required dependencies and subtasks. Record migration/backfill compatibility and rollback results when schemas change. Demonstrate the workflow in the integrated staging environment, identifying deployed build and service versions; local checks alone are not staging evidence. Production deployment remains a separate release gate under AIN-1/12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "6. For external-system or monetary settlement claims, attach configured vendor/provider-sandbox evidence and matched reconciliation; simulated events or manually recorded receipts cannot establish external delivery or settled cash."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Generated-form gate: preserve document-driven extensibility, evidence anchors, stable semantic/entity IDs, missing/conflicting states and human corrections; pin schema/catalog/generator versions, reject unsafe generated structures and prove regeneration/replay behavior. LLM output never independently grants authority, approves coverage, sets eligibility or posts money."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Completion boundary"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Backlog planning only on 2026-11-04. No implementation, test execution, migration or deployment is claimed. Assignee, estimates and dates remain for delivery planning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Resolved delivery map \u2014 persona feedback 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Implementation ownership"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Required implementation tasks/slices: AIN-18, AIN-50, AIN-51. Reuse existing completed work, implement and verify the remaining acceptance criteria in this story. Relates links identify shared ownership; Blocks links identify ordered predecessor outcomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Predecessor stories"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AIN-87"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Verification mapping"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Before Done, replace the pending evidence with actual component paths, Storybook story IDs, execution commands/results, Docker integration evidence and staging build IDs. Evidence is currently NOT RUN; no synthetic result is claimed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Target candidate: AIN S11 | Safe regeneration and activation (Jira sprint 46)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sprint outcome: Connect effective financial revisions and preserve human corrections during regeneration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Exit evidence: Stable semantic/entity matching survives reorder; material changes identify stale pricing/quotes/approvals; one effective revision and historical replay are proven."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Planning envelope: 6 implementation days + 2 integrated verification days + 1 review/refinement day + 1 contingency day; not measured velocity. One primary outcome in progress; at most two closely related workflow slices. Story/task pairs share effort, not double-counted work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scheduling is not implementation: original AC/DoD and parent scope are unchanged. Related story/task/subtask effort is one delivery slice, not additive capacity. Required domain slices can be delivered earlier than the broader owner completion sprint; no broader item is Done until all original requirements pass."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
